{"id": "767d5459-6bc3-43ea-b12a-8b4ee04cee90", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T20:17:31.835285", "source": "environment", "tool_name": "file_editor", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9593d5dc15a1e32a", "observation": {"content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on ~/owl-repro-work/P61-20261118T011646Z/openhands-gemma-4-31b-owl/workspace/OWL_SPEC.json:\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"paper_id\": \"P61\",\n     3\t  \"criteria\": {\n     4\t    \"architecture\": {\n     5\t      \"criterion\": \"architecture\",\n     6\t      \"status\": \"SPECIFIED\",\n     7\t      \"completeness\": \"FULL\",\n     8\t      \"value\": \"WiFi-based adaptation of FAB-MAP using Chow-Liu trees for joint probability distribution of re-observation of a place given WiFi fingerprint features\",\n     9\t      \"explanation\": \"The method adapts the FAB-MAP visual place recognition algorithm to WiFi fingerprints, using Chow-Liu trees to estimate the joint probability distribution.\",\n    10\t      \"uncertainties\": [],\n    11\t      \"source\": \"PAPER\",\n    12\t      \"code_evidence\": [\n    13\t        {\n    14\t          \"path\": \"src/main.cpp\",\n    15\t          \"line_range\": [\n    16\t            354,\n    17\t            356\n    18\t          ],\n    19\t          \"cell_index\": null,\n    20\t          \"quote\": \"of2::ChowLiuTree tree;\\n\\ttree.add(trainEnvDescs);\\n\\tclTree = tree.make((double)fsSettings[\\\"ChowLiuOptions\\\"][\\\"LowerInfoBound\\\"]);\"\n    21\t        }\n    22\t      ],\n    23\t      \"paper_evidence\": [\n    24\t        {\n    25\t          \"page\": 1,\n    26\t          \"quote\": \"we propose a WiFi-based global localization method employing the structure of the well-known FAB-MAP visual place recognition algorithm. Similarly to FAB-MAP, our method uses Chow-Liu trees to estimate a joint probability distribution of re-observation of a place given a set of features extracted at places visited so far