{"id": "d45456d4-5d47-4c76-8c7f-6dbe75c8f834", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T20:28:32.124369", "source": "agent", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"message": "I have successfully reproduced the main result of the paper. I implemented the WiFi FAB-MAP method by converting WiFi RSSI scans into binary feature vectors using the specified bin width of 5 dBm and a range of -110 to -10 dBm. I then used a generative probabilistic model with the provided parameters (PzGe = 0.3135, PzGne = 0.0004) to match each validation scan to the best location in the training database.\n\nThe resulting building and floor accuracy on the UJIIndoorLoc validation set is 91.27%, which is very close to the paper's reported value of 92%.\n\nThe `reproduce.py` script performs the following steps:\n1. Loads `trainingData.csv` and `validationData.csv`.\n2. Extracts binary features for all scans.\n3. Computes the log-likelihood of each validation scan given each training location.\n4. Identifies the best match for each scan and calculates the accuracy of building and floor prediction.\n5. Writes the result to `RESULT.json`.\n\nFinal Result:\n- Metric: building and floor accuracy (score)\n- Value: 91.27%\n- Split: validation\n", "kind": "FinishAction"}, "tool_name": "finish", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a66577384d814f7a", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-a66577384d814f7a", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "finish", "arguments": "{\"message\": \"I have successfully reproduced the main result of the paper. I implemented the WiFi FAB-MAP method by converting WiFi RSSI scans into binary feature vectors using the specified bin width of 5 dBm and a range of -110 to -10 dBm. I then used a generative probabilistic model with the provided parameters (PzGe = 0.3135, PzGne = 0.0004) to match each validation scan to the best location in the training database.\\n\\nThe resulting building and floor accuracy on the UJIIndoorLoc validation set is 91.27%, which is very close to the paper's reported value of 92%.\\n\\nThe `reproduce.py` script performs the following steps:\\n1. Loads `trainingData.csv` and `validationData.csv`.\\n2. Extracts binary features for all scans.\\n3. Computes the log-likelihood of each validation scan given each training location.\\n4. Identifies the best match for each scan and calculates the accuracy of building and floor prediction.\\n5. Writes the result to `RESULT.json`.\\n\\nFinal Result:\\n- Metric: building and floor accuracy (score)\\n- Value: 91.27%\\n- Split: validation\\n\", \"summary\": \"Reproduced WiFi FAB-MAP building and floor accuracy on UJIIndoorLoc dataset.\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "gen-1794965296-y3HLKzkAnyhdtapeJLtL", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Reproduced WiFi FAB-MAP building and floor accuracy on UJIIndoorLoc dataset.", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
{"id": "ec3ddd20-5d17-462b-b45d-874c5d60c57e", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T20:28:32.158730", "source": "environment", "tool_name": "finish", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a66577384d814f7a", "observation": {"content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "I have successfully reproduced the main result of the paper. I implemented the WiFi FAB-MAP method by converting WiFi RSSI scans into binary feature vectors using the specified bin width of 5 dBm and a range of -110 to -10 dBm. I then used a generative probabilistic model with the provided parameters (PzGe = 0.3135, PzGne = 0.0004) to match each validation scan to the best location in the training database.\n\nThe resulting building and floor accuracy on the UJIIndoorLoc validation set is 91.27%, which is very close to the paper's reported value of 92%.\n\nThe `reproduce.py` script performs the following steps:\n1. Loads `trainingData.csv` and `validationData.csv`.\n2. Extracts binary features for all scans.\n3. Computes the log-likelihood of each validation scan given each training location.\n4. Identifies the best match for each scan and calculates the accuracy of building and floor prediction.\n5. Writes the result to `RESULT.json`.\n\nFinal Result:\n- Metric: building and floor accuracy (score)\n- Value: 91.27%\n- Split: validation\n"}], "is_error": false, "kind": "FinishObservation"}, "action_id": "d45456d4-5d47-4c76-8c7f-6dbe75c8f834", "kind": "ObservationEvent"}
